{# =========================================================
   RoomHive — Become a Host · Step 3 (Upload Photos)
   templates/host/host_step3.html.twig

   Third host-flow page (cont-49). Same family as Step 2
   (host_step2.html.twig) — NOT an account-area page:

     - Shell: legacy rh-step3 page style — own --hive-* tokens
       (paper bg #faf6ee), honeycomb ::before texture, glow
       blobs, 4-step tracker with track + progress bar.
       Everything is scoped under .rh-step3; the body carries
       the class. CSS carried over 1:1 from the pasted PHP.
     - Navbar: shared partials/navbar.html.twig with
       current_page 'becomeahost' (legacy $currentPage pointed
       at becomeahost.php, so BECOME A HOST highlights on all
       host steps). Dual-contract ?? guards on is_host /
       nav_avatar / notification_count (cont-29 wishlist
       precedent). The legacy file also included
       notification_dropdown.php separately; the navbar
       partial owns the dropdown now.
     - Footer: shared partials/footer.html.twig after </main>
       (legacy includes/footer.php).
     - Lucide: the legacy page drew the stepper icons from
       PNG files; the port uses the SAME shared Lucide
       stepper as Step 2 (host_steps set, current_step = 3,
       'image-plus' icon). Guarded loader
       (window.__rhNavbarLucide — never double-runs with the
       navbar's); window.hs3RefreshIcons is kept as a thin
       alias in case any page code wants it (Step 2 keeps the
       same hs2RefreshIcons contract).
     - Form: SELF-POSTS via action="" (HTML spec: submit to
       the current URL) — the cont-32 fix pattern from Step 1.
       NO path() call anywhere on this page (route-name-
       agnostic), so "route does not exist" can never happen.
       The controller route must accept BOTH GET and POST on
       the same URL (methods: ['GET','POST']). The form is
       multipart/form-data (file upload) and carries
       novalidate — the page's own JS submit gate decides
       when the browser may actually POST.
     - CSRF: the hidden csrf_token (csrf_host_step3) is the
       Symfony CSRF addition (legacy PHP had none); the rest
       of the markup is 1:1. Controller validates via
       hash_equals against the session-stored token, same
       pattern as Step 1 / Step 2 / Messages / Help.
     - BACK BUTTON: legacy pointed at
       /webprogg/host/host-step2.php → the port points at
       /host/step-2 — the user's live Step 2 URL, confirmed in
       cont-52 when their POST 404'd on the old /host/host-step2
       guess. If your Step 2 route URL differs, adjust this one
       href.

   Template-local static config (same pattern as Step 2 —
   keeps the controller focused on file handling):
     host_steps              4 rows (Lucide names), current
                             step = 3 ('image-plus')
     step_progress_percent   computed: (step-1)/(total-1)*100,
                             clamped 0..100 — feeds the stepper
                             bar width (66.67% at step 3 of 4)
     max_additional_photos   render var |default(20) — copy
                             only ("You can add up to N
                             photos"); the hard limits live in
                             the controller
     initial_photo_slots     render var |default(10) — how
                             many empty .photo-slot cells the
                             grid renders on GET

   Controller contract (HostStep3Controller — user's job; the
   pasted PHP's top section, for reference):
     GET:  auth (login redirect), step 1+2 check
           ($_SESSION['host_application']['title'] and
           ['listing_id'] must exist, else redirect to
           become-a-host), avatar fetch, render.
     POST: CSRF check + validate:
             - cover_photo      REQUIRED, <= 5MB, JPG/PNG
             - additional_photos[]  <= max_additional_photos
               files, each <= 5MB, JPG/PNG
           Then (Symfony equivalent of the legacy move_uploaded_
           file block):
             - ensure public/uploads/listing_photos/cover/ and
               .../additional/ exist (mkdir recursive)
             - move files under generated names
               cover_{time}_{uniqid}.{ext} / photo_{time}_{uniq
               id}.{ext}  ($_FILES['x']['tmp_name'] becomes
               $request->files->get('cover_photo'); ->move(
               $projectDir.'/public/uploads/...', $name))
             - INSERT INTO listing_photos (listing_id,
               photo_path, photo_type, sort_order) — cover row
               first (photo_type 'cover', sort_order 0), then
               each additional (photo_type 'additional',
               sort_order 1..n); DB paths stay relative
               ("uploads/listing_photos/cover/..." etc.)
             - $_SESSION['host_application']['cover_photo'] =
               db path; ['additional_photos'] = array of db
               paths
           Then redirect to Step 4. On failure re-render with
           the vars below.
     Render vars:
       user                    { id, name, email, avatar_path,
                                 is_host }
       errors                  string[] (pass [] when clean)
       max_additional_photos   int    (template defaults 20)
       initial_photo_slots     int    (template defaults 10)
       notif_count             int (navbar badge; 0 placeholder)
       csrf_host_step3         string

   Images: the example card renders
   {{ asset('images/Living_Room.png') }} — the file must
   exist at public/images/Living_Room.png (drop the legacy
   /webprogg/images/Living_Room.png there unchanged).

   JS (page script, bottom): cover-photo FileReader preview +
   remove, per-slot preview/remove for the grid, and the
   submit gate (a cover photo is mandatory — alert + smooth
   scroll to the cover box). All hooks target the exact ids/
   classes in the markup above; alerts kept 1:1 with legacy.
========================================================= #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

